const host=document.createElement('section');host.id='analysis-extension';host.innerHTML=`<div class="ax-head"><span>NEW · 新增分析</span><h2>Explore pathways, compare cases, explain differences</h2><p>Existing charts are unchanged. These views use the full eligible sample, not a fixed set of 20 countries.</p></div><div class="ax-controls"><label>Start year <select id="ax-start"></select></label><label>End year <select id="ax-end"></select></label><label>Region <select id="ax-region"><option>All</option></select></label><label>Income group <select id="ax-group"><option value="all">All classified economies</option><option value="high">High income</option><option value="other">Low / middle income</option></select></label><label>Pathway <select id="ax-path"><option value="all">All pathways</option><option value="0">GDP↑ CO₂↓</option><option value="1">GDP↑ CO₂↑ slower</option><option value="2">GDP↑ CO₂↑ faster / equal</option><option value="3">GDP↓ CO₂↓</option><option value="4">Other / flat GDP</option></select></label><button id="ax-clear">Clear brush selection</button></div><p id="ax-status" aria-live="polite"></p><article><h3 class="ax-title">NEW · 01 Growth–carbon pathway explorer</h3><p>Drag to select countries; Shift + click a point to choose country B. Click normally to choose A. Selection filters views 02, 04 and 05.</p><div id="ax-scatter" class="ax-plot"></div></article><article><h3 class="ax-title">NEW · 02 Selected-country trend matrix</h3><div class="ax-controls"><label>Sort <select id="ax-sort"><option value="co2">CO₂ change ↓</option><option value="gdp">GDP change ↓</option><option value="name">Country A–Z</option></select></label><label>Page <select id="ax-page"></select></label></div><p>12 countries per page; common index scale across the filtered sample. Teal = GDP; orange = CO₂. Click a country heading to inspect it as A.</p><div id="ax-matrix"></div></article><article><h3 class="ax-title">NEW · 03 Kaya endpoint contribution waterfalls</h3><div class="ax-controls"><label>Country A <select id="ax-a"></select></label><label>Country B <select id="ax-b"></select></label></div><p>Contributions are cumulative log changes ×100, not percentage-point changes. GDP + energy intensity + energy carbon intensity = CO₂ change. Descriptive accounting, not causal attribution.</p><div class="ax-pair"><div id="ax-water-a" class="ax-plot"></div><div id="ax-water-b" class="ax-plot"></div></div></article><article><h3 class="ax-title">NEW · 04 Pathway composition by income group</h3><div id="ax-composition" class="ax-plot"></div></article><article><h3 class="ax-title">NEW · 05 Structural-factor distributions</h3><label>Factor <select id="ax-factor"><option value="ei">Energy intensity change (%)</option><option value="ci">Energy carbon intensity change (%)</option><option value="coal">Coal share change (percentage points)</option><option value="services">Services share change (percentage points of GDP)</option></select></label><p>Each dot is one economy; diamonds show group medians. Only matched endpoint observations are used; sample sizes are shown separately.</p><div id="ax-factors" class="ax-plot"></div></article><p class="ax-note">Grouping: World Bank FY2024 high vs low/middle income, consistent with the existing data. These are income groups, not IMF development categories. Pathways use positive endpoint GDP and CO₂; intermediate missing years remain gaps. Percentage changes describe per-person measures. Source CSVs and existing charts are unchanged.</p>`;
